<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Weil der Stadt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Weil der Stadt is a small town west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, on the river Würm. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> possession, it became a free imperial city in the 13th century and kept that status until 1803, when it passed to Württemberg. The astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler">Johannes Kepler</a> was born there in 1571.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/weil-der-stadt.jpg" alt="Weil der Stadt" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. MarkusHagenlocher assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WdSt-PeterundPaul.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
